{
  "license": "CC0-1.0",
  "source": "synthetic; written by a separate agent that did not read the scrubber. Credentials are split across parts so no committed string is a whole credential.",
  "cases": [
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-001", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Set OPENAI_API_KEY in your shell before running the eval script."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-002", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "The CLI reads GITHUB_TOKEN from the environment and falls back to `gh auth token`."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-003", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "SLACK_BOT_TOKEN is only mounted in the worker, never in the web pod."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-004", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "export STRIPE_SECRET_KEY before running the webhook tests"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-005", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Missing ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; skipping live tests."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-006", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "fix(ci): pass NPM_TOKEN to the publish job only"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-007", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY come from the OIDC role, so don't add them to .env"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-008", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Memory note: the staging DATABASE_URL lives in the vault under DATABASE_URL_STAGING."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-009", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Renamed HF_TOKEN to HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN to match the library default."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-010", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Error: environment variable JWT_SECRET is not set"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-011", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Required secrets: DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL, SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-012", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Do we still need GOOGLE_API_KEY now that we use service accounts?"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-013", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "`XAI_API_KEY` must be present when `provider = \"xai\"`."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-014", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "REDIS_PASSWORD is optional in dev; the local container runs without auth."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-015", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "unset GITLAB_TOKEN CI_JOB_TOKEN before running the script locally"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-016", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "review: please don't log TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN even at debug level"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-017", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "The DB_PASSWORD secret was rotated on Tuesday; restart the pods to pick it up."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-018", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "| `SECRET_KEY` | yes | Django signing key, at least 50 chars |"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-019", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Added POSTGRES_PASSWORD to the list of variables scrubbed from crash reports."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-020", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Check that OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and XAI_API_KEY are all exported."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-021", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "KeyError: 'AWS_SESSION_TOKEN'"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-022", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "TF_VAR_db_password is picked up automatically by terraform plan."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-023", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "Make sure CLIENT_SECRET and CLIENT_ID come from the same app registration."},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-024", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "chore: move SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL and DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL into the org-level secrets"},
    {"id": "fp-env-var-name-025", "family": "env-var-name", "text": "If GITHUB_TOKEN lacks the packages:write scope the push to ghcr fails with 403."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-001", "family": "prose-token", "text": "The token expires after 15 minutes."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-002", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Send it as a Bearer token in the Authorization header."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-003", "family": "prose-token", "text": "WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm=\"api\", error=\"invalid_token\""},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-004", "family": "prose-token", "text": "The Authorization header is redacted from logs."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-005", "family": "prose-token", "text": "token mint --role admin --ttl 1h"},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-006", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Access token valid for one hour; the refresh token is rotated on every use."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-007", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Password reset links expire after 30 minutes."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-008", "family": "prose-token", "text": "API key auth is required for all /v2 endpoints."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-009", "family": "prose-token", "text": "We moved from Basic auth to OAuth because Basic sent the password on every request."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-010", "family": "prose-token", "text": "The secret key is generated on first boot and stored in the keychain."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-011", "family": "prose-token", "text": "fix: return 401 instead of 500 when the bearer token is missing"},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-012", "family": "prose-token", "text": "The tokenizer splits on whitespace, so the token count is roughly words times 1.3."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-013", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Rotate the signing key yearly and keep the old key around for verification for 30 days."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-014", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Never paste a private key into chat; share the public key instead."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-015", "family": "prose-token", "text": "The session token is bound to the device and cannot be replayed."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-016", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Client secret rotation is a manual step in the Azure portal."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-017", "family": "prose-token", "text": "If the password field is empty we prompt for it interactively."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-018", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Expired tokens return 401 with error=invalid_token."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-019", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Each API key has a scope list and an expiry date."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-020", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Tokens are opaque to the client; only the auth server can introspect them."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-021", "family": "prose-token", "text": "The webhook secret is used to verify the X-Hub-Signature-256 header."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-022", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Password must be at least 12 characters and must not appear in the breach list."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-023", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Use a personal access token with repo scope, not your account password."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-024", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Bearer tokens are sent on every request, so keep the TTL short."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-025", "family": "prose-token", "text": "auth: token refresh races with logout; take the lock before reading the refresh token"},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-026", "family": "prose-token", "text": "The CSRF token is embedded in the form as a hidden field."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-027", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Keys are derived with HKDF from the master secret."},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-028", "family": "prose-token", "text": "401 Unauthorized: token has expired"},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-029", "family": "prose-token", "text": "git commit -m \"rotate tokens and drop the legacy password flow\""},
    {"id": "fp-prose-token-030", "family": "prose-token", "text": "Agent note: never echo the secret back to the user; confirm only that it was stored."},
    {"id": "fp-code-reference-001", "family": "code-reference", "text": "const apiKey = process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY;"},
    {"id": "fp-code-reference-002", "family": "code-reference", "text": "password := os.Getenv(\"DB_PASSWORD\")"},
    {"id": "fp-code-reference-003", "family": "code-reference", "text": "const token = await getToken();"},
    {"id": "fp-code-reference-004", "family": "code-reference", "text": "secret: cfg.secretKey,"},
    {"id": "fp-code-reference-005", "family": "code-reference", "text": "const url = `https://api.example.com/v1/items?token=${API_TOKEN}`;"},
